# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Run artefacts: logs and mid-run checkpoints are machine-specific noise.
# Final result CSV/JSON and figures ARE committed: they are the scientific
# record and should travel with the code.
results/*.log
results/**/*.partial.csv
results/_*/
# Staging folder for one-off verification reruns (compared, then deleted).
results/verify/

# Large cached datasets. They now live in datasets/ inside the project, moved
# there off the system drive by scripts/use_local_datasets.py, so this entry
# is what stops 12 GB of EEG from reaching the remote.
datasets/
mne_data/

# LaTeX build products. The compiled PDF IS tracked: it is the artefact
# people actually want to read, and a reader should not need a TeX toolchain
# plus the non-CTAN IOP class files just to see the manuscript. Everything
# else in build/ is intermediate.
paper/build/*
!paper/build/main.pdf
!paper/build/supplementary.pdf
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.out
*.log
*.xdv
# latexmk's own bookkeeping, and the PDFs it writes next to the source. The
# tracked PDFs are the ones run.py publishes into paper/build/, so these are
# duplicates that change on every rebuild.
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
paper/main.pdf
paper/supplementary.pdf

# Third-party IOP files, fetched by paper/get_iop_class.sh from IOP's own
# package and not redistributed here.
paper/iopjournal.cls
paper/orcid.pdf
paper/iopart-num.bst
paper/iopart_num.bst
# The IOP template zip as downloaded by hand from IOP's site.
ioplatextemplate.zip
# Legacy: the manuscript used iopart until 2026-09-05. Kept so a stale
# checkout does not accidentally commit them.
paper/iopart.cls
paper/iopart1*.clo
paper/iopams.sty
paper/setstack.sty
paper/harvard.sty

# Screening/smoke outputs. Superseded by the tagged production runs; keeping
# them invites quoting a 2-subject pilot as if it were the n=30 result.
results/*_smoke.csv
results/exp_*.csv

# Working notes that belong to the authors, not to the public record:
# correspondence trackers, authorship bookkeeping and local tool config.
private/
/CLAUDE.md
presentation.zip
# Talk slides and the plain-language explainer: made for the authors'
# own use, not part of the public record.
presentation/
# Correspondence with the journal: not part of the public record.
paper/cover_letter.tex
